<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Longarus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Longarus was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dardanians">Dardani</a>, the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a>, in the 3rd century BCE. He fought the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> in the 230s BCE, taking advantage of its troubles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-nicator">Demetrius II</a>. His son Bato later allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against Philip V.</p></div>
